---
import type { Country } from '../../data/countries';

interface Props {
  country: Country;
}

const { country } = Astro.props;
const { miles, cashOff, cashSymbol } = country.perks;
---
<section class="bg-white">
  <div class="container-narrow py-16 sm:py-20 max-w-3xl">
    <h2 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-medium mb-6">
      Why use a Tesla referral code in the {country.name}?
    </h2>
    <div class="prose prose-tesla text-base text-tesla-black leading-relaxed space-y-4">
      <p>
        Tesla's referral programme is the only way to get an official discount on a
        new Tesla. Tesla does not run public discount codes or sales. The referral
        benefit is the single legitimate price reduction available to UK buyers,
        and it's only unlocked when you order through an existing Tesla owner's
        referral link.
      </p>
      <p>
        For Model 3 and Model Y orders, the benefit is <strong>{miles} miles of free
        Supercharging</strong>. That's enough free charging to cover roughly 1,500
        miles of real-world driving, worth around {cashSymbol}120 at current
        Supercharger pricing, and a useful credit for early road trips while you're
        getting used to the car.
      </p>
      <p>
        For Model S and Model X orders, the benefit is <strong>{cashSymbol}{cashOff}
        off the purchase price</strong>, applied automatically at checkout. You'll
        see it deducted in your Tesla account before you confirm the order.
      </p>
      <p>
        Using a referral code costs you nothing. It doesn't change the price you
        pay or the spec of the car. It just unlocks the benefit. The owner of the
        referral code (in this case, an existing UK Tesla driver) receives a
        matching reward from Tesla. That's how the programme is designed.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
